    "content": "The President of Puntland, Said Abdullahi Deni, accompanied by a high-level delegation, has called for an immediate cessation of hostilities among clans in the Towfiq region. The appeal was made during an official visit aimed at addressing recurring violence that has displaced families and disrupted livelihoods.\n\nDeni's visit underscores the administration's concern over the cyclical nature of clashes, which have historically stemmed from disputes over resources and political representation. By engaging directly with community elders and local leaders, the president seeks to broker a sustainable peace agreement that would prevent further escalation.\n\nThe Towfiq area has seen intermittent fighting over the past years, with attempts at mediation yielding temporary truces. This latest initiative reflects a broader strategy by the Puntland government to stabilize volatile districts, which are also vulnerable to external threats from extremist groups exploiting local grievances.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the stability of regions like Towfiq is closely tied to investment and remittance flows. Many diaspora members own property or fund businesses in their home areas, making peace a prerequisite for economic growth. The president's plea is expected to resonate among those who have been advocating for grassroots conflict resolution.\n\nAs the delegation continues its tour, observers remain cautiously optimistic that this high-level engagement will produce concrete outcomes. The call for peace, however, must be matched by tangible measures, including the deployment of neutral security forces and the establishment of a reconciliation framework.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/madaxweyne-deni-oo-reer-towfiiq-ugu-baaqay-in-la-joojiyo-colaadaha-soo-laalaabtay/425118/",
